<div class="cell">
	<article class="grid-card-news">
		<div class="content">
			<div>
							<h3 class="h4">Why is there a link between height and schizophrenia?</h3>
								<p>It has been known since 1936 that people diagnosed with schizophrenia are on average 1 centimeter shorter than people without that diagnosis. However, there have been few explanations of this relationship. Neuroscientist Cato Romero and his colleagues therefore investigated the link between schizophrenia and height in DNA datasets.</p>
							</div>
		</div>
		<header class="card-header">
				<picture>
		<source data-lazy-srcset="https://cncr.nl/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Cato-Romero-13-3-2025-300x143.jpg" media="(max-width: 680px)"/>
		<source data-lazy-srcset="https://cncr.nl/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Cato-Romero-13-3-2025-300x143.jpg" media="(min-width: 680px)"/>
		<img
		 src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%200%200'%3E%3C/svg%3E"
